  "releaseNotes": "v1.3.1: Unified Backend Architecture and Major Algorithm Improvements\n- NEW: Unified IQuantumBackend interface - all quantum algorithms now work seamlessly across all backends\n- NEW: Atom Computing Phoenix backend with 100+ qubit support and comprehensive gate set\n- NEW: Quantinuum backend with dynamic qubit limits and improved documentation\n- REFACTOR: Grover, QFT, QPE, Shor's, HHL algorithms migrated to unified backend API (removed old adapters)\n- REFACTOR: Quantum arithmetic operations now use state-based architecture for better composability\n- IMPROVED: QRNG API with comprehensive documentation and examples\n- IMPROVED: Visualization system with ASCII and Mermaid renderers for circuits and solutions\n- IMPROVED: Enhanced quantum chemistry support with fermion mapping tests\n- FIXED: Circuit transpilation improvements for multi-backend compatibility\n- IMPROVED: Backend capability detection and validation\n- Status: 1400+ tests passing in main package, production-ready",
